This repository carries no third-party code. The DOS machine in src/ began as
a copy of the one in the Blake Stone recomp (https://github.com/sp00nznet/blakestone),
by the same author under the same licence. The presenter (src/present.c)
began as the Gunman Chronicles recomp's (https://github.com/sp00nznet/gunman),
and the settings menu, the blurred bars and the Linux setup (setup.sh,
build-linux.sh) follow the Red Alert 2 recomp's
(https://github.com/sp00nznet/redalert2-recomp): same author, same licence.

It builds against, but does not include, the pcrecomp toolkit (MIT):
https://github.com/sp00nznet/pcrecomp
On Linux it links the system's SDL2 (zlib licence), which is not included either.

Epic Pinball is commercial software (Epic MegaGames, 1993; sold today by GOG).
The MASI sound drivers it ships are Joshua C. Jensen's. Neither the game, nor
anything generated from its executables or drivers, is part of this repository.
